<quiz>
<question type="stack">
<name>
<text>Would like develop quiz introductory university</text>
</name>
<questiontext format="html">
<text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the definite integral \(\displaystyle\int_0^1 \frac{2x}{(x^2+{@a@})(x^2+{@b@})}\,dx\).</p>
<p>Hint: consider the substitution \(u=x^2\).</p>
<p>Enter the exact value (not a decimal approximation).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt_ans1]]</p>]]></text>
</questiontext>
<questionvariables>
<text>a: rand(5)+1;
b: a+1+rand(6-a);
ta1: (1/(b-a))*ln(b*(1+a)/(a*(1+b)));
wrong1: ln(b*(1+a)/(a*(1+b)));
wrong2: (1/(b-a))*ln(a*(1+b)/(b*(1+a)));</text>
</questionvariables>
<generalfeedback format="html">
<text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(u=x^2\), so \(du=2x\,dx\). The limits stay 0 and 1, so the integral becomes \(\int_0^1 \frac{du}{(u+{@a@})(u+{@b@})}\).</p>
<p>Partial fractions give \(\frac{1}{(u+{@a@})(u+{@b@})}=\frac{1}{{@b-a@}}\left(\frac{1}{u+{@a@}}-\frac{1}{u+{@b@}}\right)\).</p>
<p>Integrating and evaluating from 0 to 1 gives \(\frac{1}{{@b-a@}}\left[\ln\frac{u+{@a@}}{u+{@b@}}\right]_0^1={@ta1@}\).</p>]]></text>
</generalfeedback>
<specificfeedback format="html">
  <text></text>
</specificfeedback>
